    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50845" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vīcĭens</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vīcĭes</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>num. adv.</i> [viginti], <i>twenty times</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">viciens centena milia passuum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. G. 5, 13 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">viciens tantum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					14, 4, 6, § 53</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">superficiem aedium aestimarunt HS. viciens,</span>”
				i. e. <i>two millions</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 4, 2, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">HS. bis et viciens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 11, 1, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non plenum modo viciens habebas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 1, 100, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
